#20 0.144 I. MEASUREMENT PARAMETERS: 
#20 0.144  --async (-a): Enables asynchronous mode in perf_analyzer. By default,
#20 0.144 	 perf_analyzer will use synchronous API to request inference. However, if
#20 0.144 	 the model is sequential then default mode is asynchronous. Specify
#20 0.144 	 --sync to operate sequential models in synchronous mode. In synchronous
#20 0.144 	 mode, perf_analyzer will start threads equal to the concurrency
#20 0.144 	 level. Use asynchronous mode to limit the number of threads, yet
#20 0.144 	 maintain the concurrency.
#20 0.144  --sync: Force enables synchronous mode in perf_analyzer. Can be used to
#20 0.144 	 operate perf_analyzer with sequential model in synchronous mode.
#20 0.144  --measurement-interval (-p): Indicates the time interval used for each
#20 0.144 	 measurement in milliseconds. The perf analyzer will sample a time interval
#20 0.144 	 specified by -p and take measurement over the requests completed
#20 0.144 	 within that time interval. The default value is 5000 msec.
