#20 0.144 	 The default is -1 indicating that the average latency is used to
#20 0.144 	 determine stability
#20 0.144  --serial-sequences: Enables serial sequence mode where a maximum of one
#20 0.144 	 request is outstanding at a time for any given sequence. The default is
#20 0.144 	 false.
#20 0.144 
#20 0.144 II. INPUT DATA OPTIONS: 
#20 0.144  -b:     Batch size for each request sent.
#20 0.144  --input-data: Select the type of data that will be used for input in
#20 0.144 	 inference requests. The available options are "zero", "random", path to a
#20 0.144 	 directory or a json file. If the option is path to a directory then
#20 0.144 	 the directory must contain a binary/text file for each
#20 0.144 	 non-string/string input respectively, named the same as the input. Each file must
#20 0.144 	 contain the data required for that input for a batch-1 request. Each
#20 0.144 	 binary file should contain the raw binary representation of the
#20 0.144 	 input in row-major order for non-string inputs. The text file should
#20 0.144 	 contain all strings needed by batch-1, each in a new line, listed in
#20 0.144 	 row-major order. When pointing to a json file, user must adhere to the
#20 0.144 	 format described in the Performance Analyzer documentation. By
#20 0.144 	 specifying json data users can control data used with every request.
#20 0.144 	 Multiple data streams can be specified for a sequence model and the
#20 0.144 	 analyzer will select a data stream in a round-robin fashion for every
#20 0.144 	 new sequence. Multiple json files can also be provided (--input-data
#20 0.144 	 json_file1 --input-data json-file2 and so on) and the analyzer will
#20 0.144 	 append data streams from each file. When using
#20 0.144 	 --service-kind=torchserve make sure this option points to a json file. Default is
#20 0.144 	 "random".
#20 0.144  --shared-memory <"system"|"cuda"|"none">: Specifies the type of the shared
#20 0.144 	 memory to use for input and output data. Default is none.
#20 0.144  --output-shared-memory-size: The size in bytes of the shared memory region to
#20 0.144 	 allocate per output tensor. Only needed when one or more of the
#20 0.144 	 outputs are of string type and/or variable shape. The value should be
#20 0.144 	 larger than the size of the largest output tensor the model is
#20 0.144 	 expected to return. The analyzer will use the following formula to
#20 0.144 	 calculate the total shared memory to allocate: output_shared_memory_size *
#20 0.144 	 number_of_outputs * batch_size. Defaults to 100KB.
#20 0.144  --shape: The shape used for the specified input. The argument must be
#20 0.144 	 specified as 'name:shape' where the shape is a comma-separated list for
#20 0.144 	 dimension sizes, for example '--shape input_name:1,2,3' indicate tensor
#20 0.144 	 shape [ 1, 2, 3 ]. --shape may be specified multiple times to
#20 0.144 	 specify shapes for different inputs.
#20 0.144  --sequence-length: Indicates the base length of a sequence used for sequence
#20 0.144 	 models. A sequence with length X will be composed of X requests to
#20 0.144 	 be sent as the elements in the sequence. The actual length of the
#20 0.144 	 sequencewill be within +/- Y% of the base length, where Y defaults to
#20 0.144 	 20% and is customizable via `--sequence-length-variation`. If
#20 0.144 	 sequence length is unspecified and input data is provided, the sequence
#20 0.144 	 length will be the number of inputs in the user-provided input data.
#20 0.144 	 Default is 20.
#20 0.144  --sequence-length-variation: The percentage variation in length of sequences.
#20 0.144 	 This flag is only valid when not using user-provided input data or
#20 0.144 	 when `--sequence-length` is specified while using user-provided
#20 0.144 	 input data. Default is 20.
#20 0.144  --sequence-id-range <start:end>: Determines the range of sequence id used by
#20 0.144 	 the perf_analyzer. The perf_analyzer will start from the sequence id
#20 0.144 	 of 'start' and go till 'end' (excluded). If 'end' is not specified
#20 0.144 	 then perf_analyzer will use new sequence id without bounds. If 'end'
#20 0.144 	 is specified and the concurrency setting may result in maintaining
#20 0.144 	 a number of sequences more than the range of available sequence id,
#20 0.144 	 perf analyzer will exit with error due to possible sequence id
#20 0.144 	 collision. The default setting is start from sequence id 1 and without
#20 0.144 	 bounds
#20 0.144  --string-length: Specifies the length of the random strings to be generated
#20 0.144 	 by the analyzer for string input. This option is ignored if
#20 0.144 	 --input-data points to a directory. Default is 128.
#20 0.144  --string-data: If provided, analyzer will use this string to initialize
#20 0.144 	 string input buffers. The perf analyzer will replicate the given string
#20 0.144 	 to build tensors of required shape. --string-length will not have any
#20 0.144 	 effect. This option is ignored if --input-data points to a
#20 0.144 	 directory.
#20 0.144  --input-tensor-format=[binary|json]: Specifies Triton inference request input
#20 0.144 	 tensor format. Only valid when HTTP protocol is used. Default is
#20 0.144 	 'binary'.
#20 0.144  --output-tensor-format=[binary|json]: Specifies Triton inference response
#20 0.144 	 output tensor format. Only valid when HTTP protocol is used. Default is
#20 0.144 	 'binary'.
#20 0.144 
#20 0.144 III. SERVER DETAILS: 
#20 0.144  -u:                                  Specify URL to the server. When using triton default is "localhost:8000" if using HTTP and
#20 0.144 	 "localhost:8001" if using gRPC. When using tfserving default is
#20 0.144 	 "localhost:8500". 
#20 0.144  -i:                                  The communication protocol to use. The available protocols are gRPC and HTTP. Default is HTTP.
#20 0.144  --ssl-grpc-use-ssl:                  Bool (true|false) for whether to use encrypted channel to the server. Default false.
#20 0.144  --ssl-grpc-root-certifications-file: Path to file containing the PEM encoding of the server root certificates.
#20 0.144  --ssl-grpc-private-key-file:         Path to file containing the PEM encoding of the client's private key.
#20 0.144  --ssl-grpc-certificate-chain-file:   Path to file containing the PEM encoding of the client's certificate chain.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-verify-peer:             Number (0|1) to verify the peer's SSL certificate. See
#20 0.144 	 https://curl.se/libcurl/c/CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER.html for the meaning of each value. Default is 1.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-verify-host:             Number (0|1|2) to verify the certificate's name against host. See
#20 0.144 	 https://curl.se/libcurl/c/CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST.html for the meaning of each value. Default is 2.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-ca-certificates-file:    Path to Certificate Authority (CA) bundle.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-client-certificate-file: Path to the SSL client certificate.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-client-certificate-type: Type (PEM|DER) of the client SSL certificate. Default is PEM.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-private-key-file:        Path to the private keyfile for TLS and SSL client cert.
#20 0.144  --ssl-https-private-key-type:        Type (PEM|DER) of the private key file. Default is PEM.
#20 0.144 
